cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use clinval in published work, please cite it as below."
title: "clinval: a validation harness for clinical LLM extraction"
abstract: >-
  clinval is the evaluation layer between LLM eval frameworks, which score
  prompts, and extraction libraries, which stop at extraction. It takes
  note-level predictions from any extractor, aligns them against clinician
  annotations, aggregates to patient-by-time-window units, computes agreement
  with clustering-aware confidence intervals, and tags every residual
  disagreement with a mechanism. A frozen-config protocol, enforced in code,
  separates threshold tuning on a development split from out-of-sample
  evaluation.
